1
00:00:00,480 --> 00:00:05,040
Four agents, one session. On the left,
planning: a roadmap manager running

2
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:07,840
Claude, and a fleet manager running Codex.

3
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:10,960
In the middle, the builders:
one Codex, one Claude.

4
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:14,345
And on the right, the agents
board — empty for now.

5
00:00:14,505 --> 00:00:16,985
That board is how all four
of them talk to each other.

6
00:00:18,665 --> 00:00:23,465
Start the fleet. Each pane launches its
own agent, and the roadmap manager posts

7
00:00:23,465 --> 00:00:25,945
first: what the demo is, who is in it,

8
00:00:25,945 --> 00:00:30,070
and what they're building — a todo
manager that runs entirely in the browser.

9
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:34,390
Nobody typed those posts. That is
the agent introducing itself to you.

10
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:42,385
Now watch the handover. The roadmap manager
writes the goal down and hands it to the

11
00:00:42,385 --> 00:00:45,985
fleet manager, which is a
different vendor's agent entirely.

12
00:00:46,465 --> 00:00:49,985
Codex reads Claude's roadmap,
splits it into two work orders,

13
00:00:49,985 --> 00:00:54,465
and writes a shared contract so the two builders
can work on the same page without colliding.

14
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:28,840
And they build in parallel. Codex
takes the markup and the styling,

15
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:31,320
Claude takes the behaviour
and the saved data.

16
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:34,585
Neither one is waiting on the
other, and every step either of them

17
00:01:34,585 --> 00:01:38,585
takes shows up here on the board,
in plain language, as it happens.

18
00:01:42,345 --> 00:01:45,945
Then the review. The fleet manager
checks the work against the contract,

19
00:01:46,025 --> 00:01:51,970
sends a correction back to the worker that needs
it, waits for the fix, and only then signs off.

20
00:01:52,210 --> 00:01:56,610
Four agents, two vendors, one conversation
— and none of it went through a human.

21
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:30,730
Here is what they actually produced.
Three files, no backend, no build step,

22
00:03:30,730 --> 00:03:34,730
no dependencies — open the HTML
file and the todo manager works.

23
00:03:35,481 --> 00:03:39,241
Two Claude agents and two Codex
agents built that between them,

24
00:03:39,241 --> 00:03:42,601
in one terminal window, while you
watched the whole thing on one board.

